    {
      "id": "effect-during-execution",
      "input": {
        "action_state": "executing"
      },
      "expected": {
        "effect_state": "indeterminate"
      },
      "source_locator": "docs/language.rst:600-604",
      "derived": true,
      "source_text": "While an *action* is being executed, it's effect is an *indeterminate* state, i.e. we\ncannot make any statement about the outcome or result. Once the action concludes, then\nwe can evaluate its effects, whether it succeeded or failed, etc. When one action is\nchained to another, the latter depends on the effects of the former, i.e. the second one\ncan only execute when the first one completes successfully.\n"
    },
