      "source_locator": "docs/language.rst:602-604",
      "derived": true,
      "source_text": "we can evaluate its effects, whether it succeeded or failed, etc. When one action is\nchained to another, the latter depends on the effects of the former, i.e. the second one\ncan only execute when the first one completes successfully.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "privilege-escalation-success",
      "input": {
        "condition": "attacker has obtained elevated privileges",
        "condition_value": true
      },
      "expected": {
        "selected_edge_property": "on_true_refs"
      },
      "source_locator": "docs/language.rst:606-610",
      "derived": true,
      "source_text": "A *condition* splits a flow into multiple paths based on evaluating an effect, e.g. if\nthe action is a privilege escalation exploit, then the condition can test whether the\nattacker has obtained elevated privileges (i.e. the exploit succeeded) or still has\nregular privileges (i.e. the exploit failed.) A condition always selects one path to\nfollow, either the ``on_true_refs`` or the ``on_false_refs``.\n"
    },
